WEBVTT

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.780
To defeat Yuma Tsukumo and Astral...

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.400
I had decided to send Gilag to the human world...

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.420
I guess it really was too much of a burden for him alone.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.650
Alit! Is Alit here?

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.590
What's the deal, Durbe?

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:37.720
Alit, I shall order you to recover the Numbers!

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.640
Go to the human world right now!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.020
W-Wait a second!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.020
Why do I have to?

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.400
I can't Duel seriously in their world!

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.740
I want nothing to do with such a boring job!

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.910
Alit...

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:59.400
I-I got you! I just gotta go, right?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.880
It's all for the sake of the Barian World.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.740
For the sake of the Barian World.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.710
I'm counting on you, Alit.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.570
Are you sure Alit can do this?

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.820
Misael...

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:17.300
If we fail to defeat Yuma Tsukumo and recover the Numbers,

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.770
there will be no future for us Barians.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.220
Leaving this to that simpleton...

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.810
Now, don't talk like that.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:28.520
Ignoring his defects,
 Alit's skills in Dueling are very reliable.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.570
Some more minor observations won't harm us either.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:38.950
Yuma... Tsukumo.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.470
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:49.440
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.150
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.500
<i>Preparations for the fight are ready</i>

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.580
<i>I can already hear the shivering of my heart</i>

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.090
<i>Been waiting this whole time</i>

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.460
<i>I may meet with defeat...</i>

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.680
<i>But that's exactly why I have to stand back up</i>

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.220
<i>Need to get stronger again</i>

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.350
<i>It's good to believe</i>

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.060
<i>The "now", more than ever before, is</i>

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.520
<i>but another limit to break down</i>

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.570
<i>I can cross with ease</i>

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:35.030
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:41.070
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.830
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.290
<i>Right here in my hand,</i>

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:50.000
<i>I'm holding a powerful trump card.</i>

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:59.050
<i>With an unbreakable heart, I face toward my dream!</i>

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:31.890
"The Ultra-Aggressive One on One Battle!!
Yuma vs. The Unyielding Warrior, Alit"

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:38.820
<i>Bringing it on was your way, your key... your key...</i>

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.650
Oh! This is pretty awesome!

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.660
<i>I'm the Duel Idol, Sanagi Chouno!</i>

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.620
<i>"The Draw With My Warm Fingertips" is now on sale!</i>

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:55.540
<i>I will attack your heart... Directly!</i>

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.880
I see, I see...! So her name's Sanagi-<i>chan</i>, is it?!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.760
So cute...!

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.170
Yo!

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:07.470
You're having quite a blast, ain't ya?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.020
Wh-Who the hell're <i>you</i>?!

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.910
What're ya talking about?

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.600
I see. It's the first time we've met in these forms.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.140
I don't know what the hell you're talking about!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.970
That cross counter...

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.290
You're...!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.540
Alit!

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.250
Long time no see!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Though you keep on failing,
you're over here watching and drooling over cute girls?

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.970
You're in pretty high spirits.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.170
Th-That's just once in a while...

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.480
I don't care if it's once in a while or not.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.680
It's not right that you forget
 your objective because of some girl!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.390
So you're saying you wouldn't react the same?

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:59.570
Obviously! Men are all about <i>Dueling</i>!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:02.620
I ain't interested in anything but Dueling!

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:06.110
Going crazy over girls is absolutely impossible with me!

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:13.660
Well, it's be a different story if an <i>angel</i>
happened to descend before me.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.850
It's pretty frustrating that I can't Duel in my true form, let alone manage to win...

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:27.380
But even if I managed to win Duels in this form,

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.940
I still couldn't recover Numbers anyhow, so forget it.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.190
Hey, watch it!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.900
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:43.710
Are you all right?

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.490
An... angel...

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.310
A-An angel appeared!

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.020
Eh?

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.730
Huh?

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.870
Milkshake.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.040
Hey, Gilag.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.200
Do you know what <i>love</i> is?

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:49.760
An angel descended right in front of me, you know.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:57.470
Gilag, I'm gonna win over
 that angel's heart no matter what.

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:00.190
...with my <i>counter</i> strategy.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.420
Huh? Counter?

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.850
He's really such an idiot!

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.800
You're...the guy from yesterday!

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:18.620
Please excuse my rudeness back then.
 Take these as my apology.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.540
<i>First, approach using light jabs...</i>

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.740
I-It's alright! No need to apologize!

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:26.960
<i>...instantly followed by a killer counter.</i>

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.340
Gangway! Gangway!

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.470
I won!

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.050
Th-The hell?

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:35.930
I'm gonna bring it...

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.140
...to 'em!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.440
Geez! That's really dangerous, you know!

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:46.820
My bad, my bad!

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.650
Wait, Tetsuo!

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.150
Please wait for me, Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.480
Hey! Kotori-<i>san</i>!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.750
Hey!

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.680
<i>First the preemptive high-impact punch...</i>

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.640
What do you think you're doing?! That's dangerous!

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:17.600
Oh my...!

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:21.350
<i>Then I just pretend I got hit by the opponent's punch...</i>

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:30.570
<i>Then, while she's still panicking, I deliver the counter!</i>

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:35.660
<i>Are you all right?</i>

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.080
<i>What a naughty lady you are...</i>

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:42.620
<i>I was so distracted by your overwhelming beauty that I lost my footing!</i>

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.020
<i>Oh, come on now...</i>

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.250
I'll go next!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.970
Gonna bring it to 'em! Let's go, Shingetsu!

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:56.890
Please wait!

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:11.150
Miss...

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:14.400
You dropped this.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.160
That isn't mine, though...

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.540
<i>Okay! And without a second's delay...</i>

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.660
<i>Please excuse me.</i>

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.120
<i>I could have sworn this feather
 fell off those angelic wings of yours.</i>

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.050
Geez! That's nasty!

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.430
My bad, my bad!

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.140
Geez!

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.110
Please wait!

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.600
Wait!

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:52.200
Shit!

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:56.780
Judging from your expression, things didn't go too well.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:10:01.080
I don't get why, but there's 
this dude who keeps getting in the way.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.800
All of my counter strategies 
were ruined because of that guy!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.620
So you got yourself a "love rival", eh?

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.750
Then, I'll tell you something good.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:16.220
Listen. Women love strong and powerful men.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.510
If you got a rival, you just kick his ass.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:22.220
Then you show her that you're the stronger man!

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.430
Kick my rival's ass?

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:25.680
Right!

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.430
The secret of love is beating your rivals!

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.650
Win. Win!

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:37.110
Kick his ass... I get it!

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.030
Mornin', morning!

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.790
Huh...? What's... this?

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.250
"Hatashijuu"

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.710
Let's see... <i>Hatashijuu</i>...

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.310
It's a Duel Challenge! 
<i>(Hatashijou)</i>

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.000
When'd <i>you</i> get here?!

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.550
It's for the best.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:09.890
So you came.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.110
Hey!

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:15.600
What do you mean by, "A serious man-to-man Duel with Kotori at stake"?!

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:19.530
What's there to ask about?! It means what it says!

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:22.530
I'm gonna kick your ass in a Duel!

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.280
Huh?

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:27.790
You gonna Duel me or are you 
gonna run with your tail through your legs?!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:28.750
What's it gonna be?!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.120
Yeah right!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:35.340
No matter what the reason, I ain't gonna wimp out from a challenge to a Duel!

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:41.280
Duel Disk, set!

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:49.250
D-Gazer, set!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.280
<i>AR Vision: Link established.</i>

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:57.170
Duel!!

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:01.280
I'll go first! My turn!

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:02.070
Draw!

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:07.680
<i>With this appearance right now,
 I'm unable to use the Chaos Xyz. </i>

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:09.040
<i>But...</i>

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:12.740
I Summon Burning Knuckler Headgear!

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:23.620
Then I activate the Magic Card,
 Boxer Entrance Announcement!

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:29.340
This card can Special Summon one "Burning Knuckler" Monster from my hand!

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:39.230
In my corner... Burning Knuckler Glass Jaw!

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:48.280
I Overlay the Level Four Burning Knuckler Headgear and Burning Knuckler Glass Jaw!

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:53.510
I build the Overlay Network with these two Monsters!

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.680
Xyz Summon!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:00.450
Gather the flame of your soul on your fists!

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:05.200
Burning Knuckler - Restrained Barbaric Soldier, Leadblow!

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:11.480
An Xyz Summon right from the start!

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.370
Be careful, Yuma.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:14.250
Astral!

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:18.520
I can feel an extraordinary pressure coming from him!

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:21.980
He could be another assassin from Barian!

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:23.620
That guy...?

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:26.200
<i>Im...Impossible!</i>

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.850
<i>That's... That's Astral!</i>

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:32.410
<i>The messenger from the Astral World!</i>

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.830
<i>Does that mean that guy is...</i>

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:39.290
<i>So that bastard's Yuma Tsukumo?</i>

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.400
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.930
<i>Now this is getting interesting.</i>

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.450
My turn! Draw!

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:58.270
I Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:06.310
Then I activate the Magic Card, 
Unprecedented Wind, from my hand!

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:13.220
With this, Gagaga Magician gains 1000 Attack Points!

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.620
Let's go, Gagaga Magician!

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.450
Attack Leadblow!

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.250
That's too naive!

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.480
I activate Leadblow's effect!

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.740
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:14:27.020 --> 00:14:29.050
it negates its destruction in battle!

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:30.970
What?!

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:33.720
But you still take the damage!

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:44.110
A decent punch, I guess.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:48.510
But now I activate Leadblow's other effect!

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:53.650
When it loses an Overlay Unit, it gains 800 Attack Points!

00:14:56.360 --> 00:15:00.000
Not only can it not be destroyed by battle, it can also increase its Attack Power?!

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.220
I end my turn with this.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.650
My turn! Draw!

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:10.020
I activate the Continuous Magic, One-On-One Battle, from my hand!

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:15.620
When damage has been inflicted to a player due to the battle between Monsters,

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.880
then it will inflict an additional 1000 points of damage to you!

00:15:19.370 --> 00:15:22.310
Here's the one-on-one between Leadblow and Gagaga Magician!

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:26.080
I'll return the damage from before five times!

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:28.250
What?

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:34.220
Yuma!

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.950
Well? How's my counter taste?

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.820
I sure felt it!

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:44.250
But that just made this thing more interesting!

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:48.140
Oh? I end my turn like that!

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.970
Here I come! My turn! Draw!

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:53.680
I Summon Dododo Warrior!

00:15:56.020 --> 00:16:01.370
By lowering this Monster's Attack Power by 500, I can Summon it without a release!

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.600
Then I activate the Magic Card, Resurrection of the Dead, from my hand!

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:08.400
Revive, Gagaga Magician!

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:15.250
Once per turn, I can change his level 
between one and eight as I like!

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:19.280
I'll change Gagaga Magician's level to six!

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:24.620
Then I Overlay the Level Six Dododo Warrior
 and Gagaga Magician!

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:29.110
With these two Monsters, I build the Overlay Network!

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:30.840
Xyz Summon!

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:35.280
With the spirit of your passion, aim for your target!

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:37.250
Gauntlet Shooter!

00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:41.280
Then I activate Gauntlet Shooter's Monster Effect!

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:45.770
By detaching one Overlay Unit,
 it destroys one Monster on the field!

00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:50.420
Say <i>what</i>?! Something like that from get go?!

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:51.850
Did you really think that'd surprise me?!

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:54.710
Trap, activate! Xyz Block!

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.940
With this card, when my opponent activates a Monster Effect,

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:04.020
by detaching one Overlay Unit from one Xyz Monster I control on the field,

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:06.000
I can negate that effect!

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.400
Not good!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:10.620
Because he just used Leadblow's Overlay Unit...

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.740
Every time Leadblow loses an Overlay Unit, it gets stronger!

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.730
3800 Attack Points!

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.970
It gets stronger every time it's attacked!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:33.570
I set two cards face-down and end my turn!

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:36.530
My turn! Draw!

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.970
About time I give you the finishing blow!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.940
Leadblow, attack Gauntlet Shooter!

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:48.250
Release the flame of punches
 liberated from your retribution!

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.620
I activate a Trap! Battle Rush!

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:56.510
This card can negate destruction
 by an opponent's Monster's attack,

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:01.940
and the Battle Damage during this battle will be inflicted to the opposing player instead!

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.680
I was waiting for that!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:04.310
What?

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:09.140
If you hadn't attacked in the first place, my counter wouldn't have been useful!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:12.510
Counter Trap, Accel Footwork, activate!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:16.310
When my opponent activates a Trap during battle,

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:18.310
it negates the activation and destroys it!

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.800
Take this! Cross Counter!

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:27.280
Now with One-On-One Battle,
 the damage Yuma receives is 2400!

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.570
That will leave him barely standing with 100 Life Points.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.710
Counter Trap, activate!

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.120
Wait, Yuma! That card is...

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.710
Xyz Cross!

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.140
This card can be activated when my opponent activates a Trap.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:45.140
I can draw one card from my deck,

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:49.880
and if it's a Monster, the Attack Points of
 the battling Monsters are switched!

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:54.050
Then my opponent's Monster's Attack Power becomes zero!

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:59.110
But... If it's something other than a Monster, you'll receive twice that damage!

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:02.110
I can't beat him if I run with my tail between my legs!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.480
Yuma!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:06.910
Gonna bring it to 'im! Draw!

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:13.800
Alrighto! It's a Monster Card!

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.840
Gauntlet Shooter, Double Cross Counter him!

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.220
I won...

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:40.360
I won!

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:42.420
I did it!

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:50.370
That's a Quick-Play Magic, KO Burn Knuckle!

00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:57.200
With that card, when a "Burning Knuckler" Monster destroys an opposing Monster in battle,

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:00.570
that Monster's Attack Power will be inflicted as damage.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:10.970
<i>If Yuma had feared the risk of failure
 and hadn't activated Xyz Cross,</i>

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:15.520
<i>he would have lost due to 
the follow-up of KO Burn Knuckle!</i>

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:18.000
<i>Yuma's reckless gamble...</i>

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:22.570
<i>No, his heart that believes in hope no matter what the dangerous circumstances,</i>

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:25.490
<i>let him grab victory by a hair's breadth.</i>

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:28.370
I did it! I did!

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:29.400
Yuma!

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:33.370
Kotori... Why?

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.970
I'm sorry!

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:37.800
I know it was for the best if I kept quiet...

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:41.380
...but I thought it was for the best if I told Kotori-<i>san</i> after all.

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:46.080
I heard from Shingetsu-<i>kun</i> that you were dueling for me...

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:49.200
Huh? Oh, well...

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:50.600
Tsukumo...

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:53.560
Yuma...

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.940
You...!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:23.220
Hey, what's wrong?

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.880
Did that hit to your head make you snap?

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.280
Stop it!

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:32.510
Don't keep fighting like this over little old m-

00:21:32.510 --> 00:21:33.450
Get lost.

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:36.450
Um...

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:38.560
Yuma Tsukumo!

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.520
Y-Yeah?

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.820
You're really interesting!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:47.740
I'm Alit, so carve my name into your heart!

00:21:48.170 --> 00:21:51.950
'Coz I'm the man who's gonna be your rival!

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:53.950
Huh?!

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.920
What the hell? You got a problem with that?

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.880
Heck no I don't!

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:07.510
What the <i>heck</i>?! This makes no <i>sense</i>!

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.680
You little...!

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:34.390
<i>Does the thought "In any case..." following</i>

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:42.060
<i>the foreboding premonition tell you to give up?</i>

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:49.650
<i>Do you laugh at your dreams, saying "impossible"?</i>

00:22:49.650 --> 00:22:56.990
<i>You must find it funny that I'm not able to laugh at it, right?</i>

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>This song supports me, so I'll do my best for you this time.
 It's my turn to sing now.</i>

00:23:13.930 --> 00:23:18.720
<i>I will vow to you here</i>

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:29.070
<i>As long as I live, you'll always be my tiny, little friend</i>

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:37.620
<i>I'll erase all those little mistakes of yours</i>

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:42.410
<i>Because I want to become an artist</i>

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:48.710
<i>Look, I like doing it 'cuz it's fun.</i>

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:54.400
The members of the Numbers Club ended up in a strange fight!

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.740
We tried having a Sports Duel Tournament to help them get along again,

00:23:58.020 --> 00:24:00.250
but will this really help them make up?

00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:03.110
Kotori, can you even Duel?

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:05.050
I can do it for something like this, at least!

00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:07.050
I have a bad feeling about this for some reason.

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:09.340
Hey, what happened to you, Kotori?!

00:24:09.850 --> 00:24:12.110
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:12.220 --> 00:24:16.470
"Kotori Chaos Xyz Changes!?
 The Tumultuous Sports Duel Tournament"

00:24:16.470 --> 00:24:19.850
I'll save you from Barian!
